def rs485
  title "RS-485 at 3.3 V: MAX3485 with switchable termination, idle bias and DE pull-down"
  about "Half-duplex RS-485 transceiver for a 3.3 V MCU: MAX3485 with DE and RE# joined and pulled down, so the driver
      stays off and the receiver on while the firmware starts; 120 Ω termination behind a DIP switch, on at the two
      nodes at the cable ends; idle (failsafe) bias of 270 Ω from A to 3.3 V and from B to ground, so an idle
      terminated bus reads 1, not noise; pull-ups on RO and DI keep the UART lines at idle while they are released
      (maker-coverage BL-10, CK-17)."
  port a "bus line A (non-inverting) – to the connector"
  port b "bus line B (inverting) – to the connector"
  port ro "receiver output – to the MCU's UART RX"
  port di "driver input – from the MCU's UART TX"
  port de "direction: DE and RE# joined – high transmits, low receives; low until the firmware drives it"
  port vcc "the transceiver's 3.3 V supply (MAX3485: 3.0–3.6 V)"
  port gnd "ground – also the ground wire that runs with the pair"
  part U1 ic MAX3485ESA+T lcsc C18148 "{as}: RS-485 transceiver MAX3485"
  part C1 capacitor CC0805KRX7R9BB104 lcsc C49678 value 100nF "{as}: 100 nF at VCC"
  part R1 resistor 0805W8F1002T5E lcsc C17414 value 10k "{as}: DE/RE# pull-down 10 k"
    notes "Driver off, receiver on from power-up until the firmware drives the pin: the MAX3485 has no internal pull
      on DE."
  part R2 resistor 0805W8F1002T5E lcsc C17414 value 10k "{as}: RO pull-up 10 k"
    notes "RO is high impedance while RE# is high (transmitting): RX stays at idle instead of floating."
  part R3 resistor 0805W8F1002T5E lcsc C17414 value 10k "{as}: DI pull-up 10 k"
    notes "TX floats until the firmware sets up the UART; held at idle, a driver enabled early sends no start bit."
  part R4 resistor 0805W8F2700T5E lcsc C17590 value 270 "{as}: idle bias A to 3.3 V, 270"
  part R5 resistor 0805W8F2700T5E lcsc C17590 value 270 "{as}: idle bias B to ground, 270"
  part R6 resistor 0805W8F1200T5E lcsc C17437 value 120 "{as}: termination 120"
  part SW1 switch DSHP01TSGET lcsc C126848 "{as}: termination on/off"
    notes "On at the two nodes at the ends of the cable, off at every node in between."
  net a 0..5.5 V U1.A R4.2 R6.1
    notes "0–5.5 V: a 5 V transceiver may drive the same bus; RS-485's common-mode range (−7 … +12 V) is not
      declared."
  net b 0..5.5 V U1.B R5.1 SW1.b1
  net term 0..5.5 V R6.2 SW1.a1
    notes "Between the termination resistor and its switch."
  net ro @vcc U1.RO R2.2
  net di @vcc U1.DI R3.2
  net de @vcc U1.2 U1.DE R1.1
  net vcc U1.VCC C1.1 R2.1 R3.1 R4.1
  net gnd U1.GND C1.2 R1.2 R5.2
  covers REQ.missing/termination REQ.value/termination REQ.value/failsafe LVL.undefined/open_drain LVL.undefined
  notes "Idle bias 270 Ω: TI SLLA272D, equation 2, RB = VBUS_min / (VAB × (1/375 Ω + 4/Z0)), gives 333 Ω for VBUS_min
      3.0 V (the MAX3485's lowest VCC), VAB 0.25 V (200 mV receiver threshold + 50 mV noise, as TI's example) and Z0
      120 Ω. The exact divider with both terminations (60 Ω) and 32 unit loads (375 Ω) holds only 218 mV with 330 Ω;
      270 Ω holds 262 mV – the design choice here. The idle bus then draws about 5.5 mA from 3.3 V."
  notes "One bias pair per bus: the bias adds 540 Ω across the pair, with both terminations 54 Ω – the load at which
      the MAX3485 guarantees VOD ≥ 1.5 V (data sheet, DC characteristics). On the other nodes of the bus leave R4 and
      R5 out (remove them from the graph)."
  notes "Termination: SW1 on at the two nodes at the cable ends, off elsewhere (SLLA272D section 6: 120 Ω, one at each
      cable end; MAX3485 Figure 21). SW1 is rated 25 mA at 24 V DC (switching life, its only current rating): a driver
      can put up to its supply (3.6 V) across the pair, 30 mA through 120 Ω when this is the bus's only termination;
      with both ends terminated the driver's current is shared. Where the node is always at an end, a fixed 120 Ω
      without the switch is the simpler choice."
  notes "edakit counts a termination only as a resistor directly across A–B or split; the 120 Ω behind SW1 is not
      seen, so REQ.missing/termination reports the bus unterminated – accept it on the A net with the reason (\"SW1
      switches 120 Ω at this end\"). REQ.value/failsafe needs a termination across the pair to compute the idle
      voltage; without one it assumes the full supply."
  notes "DE and RE# joined: the node cannot hear its own transmission; for that, give RE# its own pin (and a
      pull-down) instead of the shared net."
  notes "Bus pins: the MAX3485 limits a shorted driver to ±250 mA and shuts down thermally (C18148 hints) – no series
      resistors on A/B. Where the bus connector is marked off_board, REQ.missing/leave asks for them anyway: the
      C18148 entry has no short_proof on A and B. For long or outdoor cables a TVS across A/B to ground (SM712 class)
      is worth a look; it is not in the block."
  notes "sim.json: the DI net under the MCU's outputs (idle high), the RO net under its inputs; a load with
      \"dip_closed\": {\"SW<n>\": [1]} simulates the termination switched on. The MAX3485 has no behaviour model: its
      supply and driver currents are not simulated."
  notes "R4 and R5, the idle bias, belong to one node of a bus: on every other node `--without R4 R5` leaves them
      out."
  set test {
      "connect": {"di": "SIG", "ro": "SIG2", "vcc": "3V3"},
      "sim": {
        "mcu": {
          "U1": {
            "outputs": ["LED_SDI", "LED_CLK", "LED_LE", "LED_OE", "SIG"],
            "inputs": ["SIG2"],
            "pullups": ["BTN"],
            "pullup_ohm": 50000}},
        "loads": {
          "t_idle": {
            "about": "UART idle (TX high), termination off",
            "gpio": {"LED_OE": 1, "SIG": 1},
            "leds_on": []},
          "t_term": {
            "about": "UART idle, termination switched on (SW2 is the block's SW1 in the example)",
            "gpio": {"LED_OE": 1, "SIG": 1},
            "dip_closed": {"SW2": [1]},
            "leds_on": []}}}}
  optional parts R4 R5
